WEBVTT

00:15.570 --> 00:18.400
I never dreamed before

00:18.400 --> 00:21.240
I'm gonna knock the door

00:21.240 --> 00:24.810
into the world of perfect free

00:24.810 --> 00:26.910
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:26.910 --> 00:29.750
You're gonna say I'm lying

00:29.750 --> 00:32.480
I'm gonna get the chance

00:32.480 --> 00:36.050
I thought a chance is far from me

00:36.050 --> 00:37.220
(You ain't no lonely!)

00:37.220 --> 00:40.130
I was made to hit in America

00:40.130 --> 00:42.990
(I was made to hit in America)

00:42.990 --> 00:48.900
I was made to hit in America

00:48.900 --> 00:52.570
You are the sun, you are the star

00:52.570 --> 00:54.570
(To me, forever)

00:54.570 --> 00:58.280
You are the sun, you are the star

00:58.280 --> 01:01.510
(To me, forever)

01:08.350 --> 01:13.960
I was made to hit in America

01:13.960 --> 01:16.800
I was made to hit in America

01:16.800 --> 01:19.660
(I was made to hit in America)

01:19.660 --> 01:22.470
I was made to hit in America

01:22.470 --> 01:25.240
(I was made to hit in America)

01:25.240 --> 01:33.110
I was made to hit in America

01:41.690 --> 01:42.810
Tanaka-kun!

01:45.120 --> 01:46.360
Huh?

01:46.360 --> 01:49.860
Tanaka-kun, I heard you're
going perform at Grateful Sound?

01:49.860 --> 01:52.860
That's so awesome! There's going
to be famous people there, right?

01:52.860 --> 01:55.300
Chiba-senpai and Sakurai-kun's
going to be there too.

01:55.300 --> 01:57.060
Umm, ah...

02:01.710 --> 02:04.380
Hey, you! Stop acting like you're all that!

02:04.380 --> 02:08.710
Yeah, just 'cause you were in some
stupid movie...You really piss us off!

02:08.710 --> 02:11.010
Jim's movie isn't stupid!

02:13.550 --> 02:17.250
Chiba's out sick today.

02:18.720 --> 02:19.950
Hey!

02:21.060 --> 02:22.650
What are you kids doing out here?!

02:24.400 --> 02:25.450
Yikes!

02:36.410 --> 02:38.080
Let me treat you.

02:38.080 --> 02:40.170
Okay, strawberry milk, please.

02:46.520 --> 02:50.860
During the second semester those guys
are gonna get beaten up by Chiba-kun.

02:50.860 --> 02:53.690
I'd rather not let
the guys know about today.

02:53.690 --> 02:55.860
Huh? But why?

02:55.860 --> 03:00.030
I'd rather not cause any more
problems for the band now.

03:00.030 --> 03:02.030
I see.

03:02.030 --> 03:03.030
Thanks.

03:03.030 --> 03:04.070
It's a month away from Grateful Sound...

03:04.070 --> 03:05.300
"Live 22 'Performance Eve Festival'"

03:04.070 --> 03:05.300
It's a month away from Grateful Sound...

03:05.300 --> 03:07.670
"Live 22 'Performance Eve Festival'"

03:05.300 --> 03:07.670
Everyone's on pins and needles.

03:07.670 --> 03:09.040
"Live 22 'Performance Eve Festival'"

03:10.390 --> 03:12.090
That one...or this...

03:17.230 --> 03:18.730
Which one's better?

03:18.730 --> 03:21.900
Let's see...I think the simple one's better.

03:21.900 --> 03:24.600
Yeah? Okay...

03:29.910 --> 03:31.910
Can you tell they're really into it?

03:31.910 --> 03:32.910
Yeah.

03:32.910 --> 03:37.520
I think they were really
inspired by your demo tape.

03:37.520 --> 03:38.850
You think so?

03:38.850 --> 03:40.820
Your song has real potential.

03:40.820 --> 03:45.190
Hey, Koyuki! It's your song, so I'm
counting on you to come up with the lyrics.

03:45.190 --> 03:48.590
We're going to blow them away
at Grateful Sound.

03:49.860 --> 03:51.260
Saku...

03:52.370 --> 03:53.390
Lyrics?

03:55.700 --> 03:58.230
What have I gotten myself into?

04:00.210 --> 04:03.710
It's been two weeks already,
and I've got nothing.

04:03.710 --> 04:05.870
Only ten more days until Grateful Sound...

04:07.710 --> 04:09.510
That feeling...

04:13.890 --> 04:15.720
If only I can remember it...

04:26.570 --> 04:29.070
Hey!

04:29.070 --> 04:31.240
Koyuki-kun!

04:31.240 --> 04:35.070
Say, Momoko-sensei and I have
decided to go on a trip together,

04:35.070 --> 04:37.840
I'm wondering if I should get circumcised.

04:37.840 --> 04:42.020
To do it or not to do it...
I feel almost like Hamlet right now!

04:42.020 --> 04:46.020
Ouch! Ouch, ouch! What are
you doing, Koyuki-kun?! Stop!

04:46.020 --> 04:48.350
I see? Writing lyrics, huh?

04:48.350 --> 04:51.190
I feel like I'm being
crushed by all this pressure.

04:51.190 --> 04:54.030
Can you let me listen to your song?

04:54.030 --> 04:55.020
Sure.

04:56.200 --> 04:57.700
Here.

04:57.700 --> 05:01.200
Aww, you should take it easy.

05:01.200 --> 05:05.140
They say Paul McCartney heard
the lyrics for "Yesterday" in a dream.

05:06.540 --> 05:08.010
A dream?

05:10.710 --> 05:13.800
That night, I dreamt this dream...

05:15.220 --> 05:16.480
"'Happy Sangokushi'
Premiere Press Conference"

05:15.220 --> 05:16.480
...Tanaka-san?

05:16.480 --> 05:19.520
"'Happy Sangokushi'
Premiere Press Conference"

05:16.480 --> 05:19.520
I hope people can learn

05:19.520 --> 05:22.220
"'Happy Sangokushi'
Premiere Press Conference"

05:19.520 --> 05:22.220
from the rhythm of my acting.

05:22.220 --> 05:24.390
"'Happy Sangokushi'
Premiere Press Conference"

05:22.220 --> 05:24.390
Please teach me kindly.

05:24.390 --> 05:24.720
Please teach me kindly.

05:24.720 --> 05:28.820
Mmm...Let's see...I think it'll
be good if you keep observing me.

05:32.400 --> 05:34.370
Yukio! Telephone!

05:35.400 --> 05:38.000
Who is it, in the middle of the night?

05:38.000 --> 05:41.000
Koyuki-kun, what should
I do about the circumcision?

05:42.010 --> 05:43.510
Hmph!

05:43.510 --> 05:43.840
To the east on the highway,

05:43.840 --> 05:45.510
"Fishing Hole"

05:43.840 --> 05:45.510
To the east on the highway,

05:45.510 --> 05:47.850
"Fishing Hole"

05:45.510 --> 05:47.850
The man riding on a snake.

05:47.850 --> 05:49.280
"Fishing Hole"

05:47.850 --> 05:49.280
...about ten miles long...

05:50.520 --> 05:53.450
These are some highbrow lyrics...

05:57.360 --> 06:00.620
...Not!! This is straight
out of Jim Morrison!

06:02.360 --> 06:06.870
Um...I'm trying my best...

06:06.870 --> 06:10.540
Hey, don't push him so hard.

06:10.540 --> 06:13.210
For us to compete at Grateful Sound,

06:13.210 --> 06:16.210
each and every one of us
has to do better.

06:16.210 --> 06:19.870
If he can't cut it,
then he should leave the band.

06:23.220 --> 06:24.770
Koyuki-kun!

06:26.550 --> 06:28.390
Hey, you seem kind of down today.

06:28.390 --> 06:31.650
You seem pretty chipper today, Saito-san.

06:32.730 --> 06:36.390
This...I gave it a shot
with my lyrics. Huh?

06:37.830 --> 06:39.800
Sa-Saito-san!

06:43.340 --> 06:49.340
By shucking off one skin,
my confidence has grown,

06:49.340 --> 06:52.850
Show your courage, trust the doctors...

06:52.850 --> 06:54.850
What the heck is this?!

06:54.850 --> 06:58.250
Is this really the work of someone who
worships the Rocket Boys and the Beatles?

07:01.020 --> 07:02.280
But then...

07:04.020 --> 07:07.360
Saito-san's not at all
embarrassed by his feelings

07:07.360 --> 07:09.560
or concerned about what others may say.

07:11.860 --> 07:15.030
Compared to him, maybe I've been
too concerned about what others think,

07:15.030 --> 07:16.700
and haven't been honest
in expressing myself.

07:16.700 --> 07:20.370
You can't reach people's hearts
by being so guarded.

07:35.220 --> 07:37.420
H-Hmm?

07:43.160 --> 07:44.690
What's that?

07:45.630 --> 07:46.630
"Dear Ryusuke,

07:46.630 --> 07:48.630
The other day, when you read
my lyrics in front of everyone,
I was really embarrassed.

07:48.630 --> 07:50.640
That's probably because those lyrics
didn't come from the heart.

07:50.640 --> 07:51.900
This time, I wrote
what came from my heart.

07:51.900 --> 07:52.610
It's tough to get criticized,
but I want to hear your honest opinion."

07:52.610 --> 07:54.210
It's tough to get criticized,
but I want to hear your honest opinion."
Hmm...That Koyuki...

07:54.210 --> 07:55.780
Hmm...That Koyuki...

07:55.780 --> 07:59.750
"...but I want to hear your honest opinion.
Please listen to the MD.

07:59.750 --> 08:04.710
This is the best I can do for now."

08:10.860 --> 08:16.850
By shucking off one skin,
my confidence has grown...

08:25.540 --> 08:30.310
Hmm...Huh? What's this?

08:57.000 --> 08:59.200
Stop! You ignored the traffic light!

09:37.310 --> 09:39.370
Hey, here's the genius!

09:42.320 --> 09:46.650
Ryusuke was so inspired by your efforts,
he wrote these lyrics.

09:46.650 --> 09:50.160
It's super straightforward,
just like you.

09:50.160 --> 09:52.990
You, you think so?

09:52.990 --> 09:55.460
But why's Saito-san singing the song?

09:56.830 --> 09:58.160
Well, ah...

09:58.160 --> 10:00.500
I liked the part about
shucking off one's skin.

10:00.500 --> 10:02.340
So I went with "Slip Out."

10:02.340 --> 10:05.740
Like how we're trying to
slip out of our current situation,

10:05.740 --> 10:07.510
to get to something better.

10:07.510 --> 10:11.340
-I like being wrapped with warmness
more than anything else for sure.

10:11.340 --> 10:13.510
-You never know what fate
-I like being wrapped with warmness
more than anything else for sure.

10:13.510 --> 10:15.210
-May bring your way...
-I'm gonna make my coming days
to be filled with laughter and joy

10:15.210 --> 10:19.390
-I'm gonna make my coming days
to be filled with laughter and joy

10:19.390 --> 10:21.290
"1. Pany

10:19.390 --> 10:21.290
2. Lovely Mouth

10:19.390 --> 10:21.290
3. Beck

10:19.390 --> 10:21.290
4. The Saw

10:19.390 --> 10:21.290
5. Hitode"

10:40.310 --> 10:42.170
Hitode really was something.

10:42.170 --> 10:44.370
Yeah, their sound was really tight.

10:45.480 --> 10:49.280
Yo! We're going out
with Hitode after the show!

10:51.820 --> 10:55.320
We auditioned for the first Grateful Sound.

10:55.320 --> 10:58.490
It was on a huge stage,
and we were nervous.

10:58.490 --> 11:00.990
We've never been more nervous.

11:00.990 --> 11:04.100
Remember this, you're going on
with no rehearsal,

11:04.100 --> 11:05.830
so your first song is
practically thrown away.

11:05.830 --> 11:12.170
Anyway, you guys are probably dead last
of the 94 participating bands.

11:13.170 --> 11:16.340
You there, was it Ryusuke?

11:16.340 --> 11:20.010
You've been scowling the whole time.
You got something against us?

11:22.680 --> 11:25.350
-Do you want to eat yu-dofu (hot tofu)?
-Huh?

11:25.350 --> 11:27.080
It's the most popular dish here.

11:36.700 --> 11:40.870
That was hot, damn it!
What the hell d'ya do that for!?

11:40.870 --> 11:42.360
Are you making fun of us?

11:44.040 --> 11:45.200
Watch out!

11:52.210 --> 11:54.550
Hey, you're disturbing
the other customers!

11:54.550 --> 11:56.140
You guys, get out!

11:57.880 --> 11:59.890
Hey, Koyuki, is your face alright?

11:59.890 --> 12:02.560
Yeah, I'm okay. That was
just a sucker punch anyway.

12:02.560 --> 12:05.820
I guess we won't be
playing with Hitode again.

12:13.570 --> 12:17.570
I can understand Ryusuke-kun
feeling edgy now, but...

12:17.570 --> 12:22.800
as much as I feel nervous about this,
I'm feeling really excited, too.

12:32.080 --> 12:34.590
That Koyuki...He's running late!

12:34.590 --> 12:40.360
Ryusuke, good luck!
Bring this charm with you.

12:40.360 --> 12:43.200
Sorry! I stopped by the drugstore
and ran a bit late.

12:43.200 --> 12:45.200
I swear...

12:45.200 --> 12:47.200
Thank you, Granny!

12:47.200 --> 12:50.190
"7/29 (Thursday) 11:00"

12:57.210 --> 12:59.210
You can sleep too, you know.

12:59.210 --> 13:01.050
Yeah, I'm okay.

13:01.050 --> 13:07.050
It seems Saku, Koyuki, and Chiba,
couldn't sleep at all last night.

13:07.050 --> 13:08.210
Me too.

13:16.730 --> 13:17.560
Wow, that was a good nap.

13:17.560 --> 13:19.230
Yeah, I got some sleep too.

13:19.230 --> 13:21.070
What, then Taira-kun?

13:21.070 --> 13:23.540
I couldn't sleep yesterday, either.

13:26.070 --> 13:27.910
Is this where we're gonna?

13:27.910 --> 13:30.580
Weren't you listening at the meeting?

13:30.580 --> 13:34.080
This is where Belle Ame,
featuring Yoshito, will be performing.

13:34.080 --> 13:36.680
The main stage
accommodates 20,000 people.

13:36.680 --> 13:39.690
There's also a second stage,
with a 16,000 capacity,

13:39.690 --> 13:43.020
and the third stage
with a 12,000 capacity.

13:43.020 --> 13:47.190
They'll have performances
simultaneously on all three stages.

13:47.190 --> 13:49.680
You can walk between the stages.

13:50.700 --> 13:53.870
They're each about 10 minutes apart.

13:53.870 --> 13:55.630
Well then, let's go!

13:55.630 --> 13:56.660
-Yeah!
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

13:59.710 --> 14:03.380
Here on the second stage, hip hop artist
Malcolm will be performing.

14:03.380 --> 14:07.610
He's a monster of an artist who's sold
over 20 million tickets in the US.

14:07.610 --> 14:11.050
Well, let's head on over to the
third stage, where we'll be performing.

14:11.050 --> 14:13.720
Um, can we take a little break?

14:13.720 --> 14:15.150
It's a cute trail.

14:15.150 --> 14:16.020
Uh-huh.

14:18.560 --> 14:21.220
Don't you think our stage is kind of far?

14:26.070 --> 14:29.240
This is where we'll be performing...
The third stage.

14:29.240 --> 14:34.070
It's the smallest of the three stages,
with a 12,000 capacity.

14:34.070 --> 14:35.100
Hey!

14:36.510 --> 14:37.640
Koyuki!

14:45.020 --> 14:49.750
I wonder how many people will come out
to see an unknown band like us?

14:51.860 --> 14:56.860
Oh, I'm so hungry! I'm dying to eat!

14:56.860 --> 15:02.370
Here's some rice balls my mom made.
They're for everyone.

15:02.370 --> 15:06.870
Alright! Delicious!

15:06.870 --> 15:10.380
Here. Koyuki's mom made these rice balls.

15:10.380 --> 15:12.110
Yeah.

15:22.890 --> 15:27.060
Sorry...I haven't been able
to eat these past few days.

15:27.060 --> 15:30.430
Koyuki, Saku, sorry.
I need to go talk to him.

15:35.900 --> 15:41.840
These were Leon Syke's terms in exchange
for our appearance at Grateful Sound...

15:41.840 --> 15:45.380
He gets all royalties for
the next 5 albums we release,

15:45.380 --> 15:50.020
and we don't get compensated for
any tours or promotions he books us on.

15:50.020 --> 15:54.190
Does this mean that Leon Sykes will
be endorsing us and we'll be famous?

15:54.190 --> 15:59.620
Idiot! He's not going to spend
his money on an unknown band like ours.

16:01.130 --> 16:02.530
It's my fault.

16:02.530 --> 16:05.000
It's repayment for the guitar
and the dog I took.

16:06.030 --> 16:08.200
He's going to stick us
with a crazy schedule,

16:08.200 --> 16:10.870
then toss us out when we're through.

16:10.870 --> 16:12.540
Probably.

16:12.540 --> 16:15.270
But I also gave him my terms too.

16:16.710 --> 16:18.010
What kind of terms?

16:43.500 --> 16:48.200
If an unknown band like us gets
most attendance out of 3 stages...

16:50.010 --> 16:51.680
What're you trying to say?

16:51.680 --> 16:55.250
If we actually got
the most number of audience...

16:55.250 --> 16:57.080
would you forget everything I did?

16:59.350 --> 17:02.860
You think you can get a bigger audience
than these major artists?

17:02.860 --> 17:05.690
Would you just shut up for a second?

17:05.690 --> 17:08.860
Yo, you think you're in
an equal position, muthafucker?!

17:08.860 --> 17:11.030
I wanna take my chances.

17:11.030 --> 17:13.160
You...Are you serious?

17:21.870 --> 17:26.050
The number of people at each stage
can be counted by the staff.

17:26.050 --> 17:28.550
That's precious marketing material.

17:28.550 --> 17:30.220
Put the gun down.

17:30.220 --> 17:35.390
Huh?! Boss, don't,
don't listen to this muthafucker.

17:35.390 --> 17:40.190
Put the gun down, okay.
Goldie, this is business.

17:45.660 --> 17:47.190
Such a gamble...

17:48.670 --> 17:52.670
Hey! There's no way
we can beat out Malcolm!

17:52.670 --> 17:56.840
When I heard Koyuki's song...
I felt a possibility.

17:56.840 --> 18:00.010
Don't go betting away
our future on your hunch!

18:00.010 --> 18:03.180
It seems that this eve of the festival

18:03.180 --> 18:05.150
is going to be quite
significant for all of us...

18:06.350 --> 18:08.290
-Rock, paper, scissors!
-Rock, paper, scissors!

18:09.360 --> 18:13.160
If you can find a pastry that's not
all stale, get it for me, will ya?

18:30.710 --> 18:32.380
Hey, if it isn't Koyuki-kun...

18:32.380 --> 18:33.880
What are you doing out here?

18:33.880 --> 18:37.820
I-I was going to go get some eye drops.

18:37.820 --> 18:40.150
Are you staying at the campsite?

18:40.150 --> 18:42.650
Uh-huh. What about you?

18:42.650 --> 18:45.210
Koyuki-kun, can you come with me awhile?

18:46.490 --> 18:50.000
I wonder which stage Maho will go see...

18:50.000 --> 18:54.170
If Maho comes to see my stage,

18:54.170 --> 18:58.170
then you give up on her
and never show your face again.

18:58.170 --> 19:02.010
And if I agreed to that,
will you do the same?

19:02.010 --> 19:03.340
You bet.

19:03.340 --> 19:06.350
Good. I wanted to clear things up too.

19:06.350 --> 19:08.410
I guess this will settle things then.

19:08.410 --> 19:09.240
Yeah.

19:15.520 --> 19:18.520
The Performance Eve Festival
has a jam session,

19:18.520 --> 19:21.590
a copying contest and all kinds of fun.

19:21.590 --> 19:25.360
Hmm. Would have been nice to participate.

19:25.360 --> 19:29.870
Hey you guys!
What are you guys doing there?!

19:29.870 --> 19:31.700
Oh, Aunty...

19:31.700 --> 19:33.870
Picking my nose.

19:33.870 --> 19:38.310
We were told that an audition band
like ours couldn't participate.

19:38.310 --> 19:41.310
Who told you such nonsense?!

19:41.310 --> 19:43.650
Ah, those were Ran-san's orders...

19:43.650 --> 19:44.820
What?!

19:44.820 --> 19:46.490
Fine. You boys come with me.

19:46.490 --> 19:49.820
We can go in? Wow, Aunty,
you've got some clout here!

19:49.820 --> 19:50.820
I told you!

19:50.820 --> 19:53.420
It was my sister who originally
put together Grateful Sound.

19:57.160 --> 19:58.990
If Maho...

20:00.000 --> 20:00.990
Hey!

20:03.000 --> 20:04.000
Dude, over here!

20:04.000 --> 20:05.770
Huh, me?

20:05.770 --> 20:08.340
Dude, I finally found you!

20:08.340 --> 20:10.540
Yeah, the guy in the movie, alright!

20:12.080 --> 20:14.010
He's...he's a small kid, man!

20:14.010 --> 20:15.180
He is small!

20:15.180 --> 20:19.690
Uh...eh...uh...
You guys are from Kneecap...

20:19.690 --> 20:21.850
Kneecap? Right.

20:21.850 --> 20:24.690
We're trying to play a Crush song
on the eve of the festival.

20:24.690 --> 20:26.780
Would you play with us, if you like?

20:27.860 --> 20:31.200
I...can't...English...

20:31.200 --> 20:32.560
Yo!

20:32.560 --> 20:34.200
Yoshito-kun?

20:34.200 --> 20:36.390
Want me to translate for you?

20:39.970 --> 20:41.910
Where the heck did Koyuki go?

20:41.910 --> 20:44.400
I wonder if he couldn't
find any pastries...

20:50.320 --> 20:51.320
Who's that kid?

20:51.320 --> 20:53.820
-Hey, isn't that the boy
in the Dying Breed movie?
-Huh?! That's him?

20:53.820 --> 20:55.320
-What was the name of their band?
-Mongo-Mongolian something?

20:55.320 --> 20:58.450
No way! He's such a little kid!
I'm bummed!

20:59.830 --> 21:04.330
Come on, Koyuki. I'm counting on you.
These people here are the core fans...

21:04.330 --> 21:06.170
If you can make an impact here tonight,

21:06.170 --> 21:08.360
they may follow us to our stage tomorrow...

21:09.500 --> 21:13.840
Beck's fate depends on you!

21:13.840 --> 21:15.400
Ooh! It's the Crush!

21:23.680 --> 21:25.170
I don't know this song.

21:30.690 --> 21:33.020
Thanks for the translation...

21:36.200 --> 21:38.160
Get off the stage!

21:38.860 --> 21:41.200
What did you say?? Damn you!

21:41.200 --> 21:43.370
Please do not throw things on to the stage!

21:43.370 --> 21:46.430
You there with the black cap,
please calm down!

21:53.050 --> 21:57.820
It was quite a while after
the festival that Saku told me.

21:57.820 --> 22:02.690
Later that night, Ryusuke defeated
his former bandmate Eiji.

22:16.240 --> 22:18.740
Yo! I got the pastries.

22:18.740 --> 22:20.070
Tomorrow's forecast?

22:20.070 --> 22:24.010
It's supposed to be sunny. With maybe
a few showers in the afternoon.

22:26.580 --> 22:27.740
I see...

22:29.410 --> 22:32.580
Let's eat some pastries together!

22:32.580 --> 22:34.920
It's not stale?

22:34.920 --> 22:36.690
Nah.

22:36.690 --> 22:38.690
Saku...

22:38.690 --> 22:39.750
Yeah.

22:43.460 --> 22:48.830
Full moon sways

22:50.300 --> 22:56.300
Gently in the night of one fine day

22:56.300 --> 22:59.010
What a fool

22:59.010 --> 23:02.480
I don't know 'bout tomorrow

23:02.480 --> 23:07.320
What it's like to be

23:07.320 --> 23:09.310
Ah...

23:10.480 --> 23:12.320
I was fool

23:12.320 --> 23:16.490
Couldn't let myself to go

23:16.490 --> 23:21.260
Even though I feel

23:21.260 --> 23:27.170
The end

23:46.120 --> 23:51.650
Full moon sways

23:52.960 --> 23:59.990
Smiling in my arms for all those years

24:13.750 --> 24:17.590
Last time, when I dove into
the audience, I fell on my head...

24:17.590 --> 24:18.820
But I didn't get hurt!

24:18.820 --> 24:19.680
A-ho!
